{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-257194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,2]\\times [0,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-2xy+3{y}^{2}+x.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,0]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n| ${x}_{1}≈[$ | {{field-1}} | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-2xy+3{y}^{2}+x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-2xy+3{y}^{2}+x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2xy-4x-2y+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+6y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy-4x-2y+1) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2x+6y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-4x-2y+1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2x+6y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2y-4 & 2x-2 \\\\ 2x-2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}2y-4 & 2x-2 \\\\ 2x-2 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2xy-4x-2y+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}2y-4 & 2x-2 \\\\ 2x-2 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2xy-4x-2y+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2(0)-4 & 2(1)-2 \\\\ 2(1)-2 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2(1)(0)-4(1)-2(0)+1 \\\\ (1)^{2}-2(1)+6(0)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(-4)\\cdot 6-(0)\\cdot (0)}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{24}[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.25 \\\\ 0.167\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fb5fb552b5d691f924559d19ffdc961443b794f7eba6de05b995ffc3b12c626"} {"question" "q-257194" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257194" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.250"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257194" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257194" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.167"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+x.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[1,\\,1]^{T}.$\n\n| $[$ | $2$ | {{field-1}} | $]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$ | $-3$ | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6xy-4x+1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6xy-4x+1) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-4y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6xy-4x+1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-4y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6y-4 & 6x \\\\ 6x & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}6y-4 & 6x \\\\ 6x & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}6xy-4x+1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}6y-4 & 6x \\\\ 6x & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}6xy-4x+1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6(1)-4 & 6(1) \\\\ 6(1) & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}6(1)(1)-4(1)+1 \\\\ 3(1)^{2}-4(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fb5fb552b5d691f924559d19ffdc961443b794f7eba6de05b995ffc3b12c626"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257202" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=7{x}^{2}y-2xy+3{y}^{3}-1.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,1]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[-1,\\,0]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n| ${x}_{2}≈[$ | {{field-1}} | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(7{x}^{2}y-2xy+3{y}^{3}-1) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(7{x}^{2}y-2xy+3{y}^{3}-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14xy-2y \\\\ 7{x}^{2}-2x+9{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(14xy-2y) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(7{x}^{2}-2x+9{y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(14xy-2y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(7{x}^{2}-2x+9{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14y & 14x-2 \\\\ 14x-2 & 18y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}14y & 14x-2 \\\\ 14x-2 & 18y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}14xy-2y \\\\ 7{x}^{2}-2x+9{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}14y & 14x-2 \\\\ 14x-2 & 18y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}14xy-2y \\\\ 7{x}^{2}-2x+9{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}14(0) & 14(-1)-2 \\\\ 14(-1)-2 & 18(0)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}14(-1)(0)-2(0) \\\\ 7(-1)^{2}-2(-1)+9(0)^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -16 \\\\ -16 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 0-(-16)\\cdot (-16)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 16 \\\\ 16 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{256}[\\begin{aligned}144 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.438 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fb5fb552b5d691f924559d19ffdc961443b794f7eba6de05b995ffc3b12c626"} {"question" "q-257211" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257211" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.438"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=4{x}^{2}y-3x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}-2x.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[1,\\,1]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration. Round the answer for ${x}_{1}$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n| $[$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ | $]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$ | $-5$ | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n\n| ${x}_{1}≈[$ | $0.594$ | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}y-3x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}-2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y-3x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}-2x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}-6xy) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}-6xy)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8y+2 & 8x-6y \\\\ 8x-6y & -6x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}8y+2 & 8x-6y \\\\ 8x-6y & -6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}8y+2 & 8x-6y \\\\ 8x-6y & -6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8(1)+2 & 8(1)-6(1) \\\\ 8(1)-6(1) & -6(1)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}8(1)(1)-3(1)^{2}+2(1)-2 \\\\ 4(1)^{2}-6(1)(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get $({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}-13/32 \\\\ -15/32\\end{aligned}].$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{13}{32} \\\\ -\\frac{15}{32}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{13}{32} \\\\ -\\frac{15}{32}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.594 \\\\ 0.531\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fb5fb552b5d691f924559d19ffdc961443b794f7eba6de05b995ffc3b12c626"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257212" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.531"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-1,2]\\times [-2,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[2,\\,-2]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[1.75,\\,0.125]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n| ${x}_{2}≈[$ | $-0.301$ | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-1}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-2xy+6x \\\\ 4xy-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{y}^{2}-2xy+6x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy-{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{2}-2xy+6x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2y+6 & 4y-2x \\\\ 4y-2x & 4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}-2y+6 & 4y-2x \\\\ 4y-2x & 4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-2xy+6x \\\\ 4xy-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}-2y+6 & 4y-2x \\\\ 4y-2x & 4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-2xy+6x \\\\ 4xy-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.75 \\\\ 0.125\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-2(0.125)+6 & 4(0.125)-2(1.75) \\\\ 4(0.125)-2(1.75) & 4(1.75)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2(0.125)^{2}-2(1.75)(0.125)+6(1.75) \\\\ 4(1.75)(0.125)-(1.75)^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.75 \\\\ 0.125\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}5.75 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}10.093\\,75 \\\\ -2.187\\,5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.75 \\\\ 0.125\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(5.75)\\cdot 7-(-3)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5.75\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10.093\\,75 \\\\ -2.187\\,5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.75 \\\\ 0.125\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{31.25}[\\begin{aligned}64.093\\,75 \\\\ 17.703\\,125\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.301 \\\\ -0.442\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fb5fb552b5d691f924559d19ffdc961443b794f7eba6de05b995ffc3b12c626"} {"question" "q-257249" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"} {"question" "q-257249" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.442"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083550/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa9c1f959eb6b66a19bf96d355f91656cea83a9e47702d3e8d8d3047a4e749bd"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2876 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
